erive\"] }     # JSON (de)serialization\nserde_json = \"1.0\"\nclipboard = \"0.5\"                                       # cross\u2011platform clipboard\nrodio = \"0.17\"                                          # audio playback\nanyhow = \"1.0\"                                          # error handling\ndotenvy = \"0.15\"                                        # optional: load .env\n```\n\n> **Why these crates?**  \n> * `tokio` \u2013 async runtime needed by `reqwest`.  \n> * `reqwest` \u2013 HTTP client with streaming support.  \n> * `serde`/`serde_json` \u2013 build the JSON request body.  \n> * `clipboard` \u2013 read the system clipboard.  \n> * `rodio` \u2013 play the audio bytes.  \n> * `anyhow` \u2013 simple error handling.  \n> * `dotenvy` \u2013 optional, lets you keep your API key in a `.env` file.\n\n---\n\n## 3. src/main.rs\n\n```rust\nuse anyhow::{anyhow, Context, Result};\nuse clipboard::ClipboardContext;\nuse rodio::{Decoder, OutputStream, Sink};\nuse serde::Serialize;\nuse std::io::Cursor;\nuse std::time::Duration;\nuse tokio::time::sleep;\n\n/// ElevenLabs TTS request payload\n#[derive(Serialize)]\nstruct ElevenLabsRequest<'a> {\n    text: &'a str,\n    voice_settings: VoiceSettings,\n}\n\n#[derive(Serialize)]\nstruct VoiceSettings {\n    stability: f32,\n   ", "Sure thing! To make the \u201cFilters\u201d section clearer and easier to read, I\u2019ll need the current version of the document (or at least the part that contains the Filters). Once I have that, I can rewrite it in a", "", "", "", "", ""], "errors": ["", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""], "max_output_tokens_per_s": 36.0, "max_concurrent_requests": 3, "rtfx": 0.0, "spec_decode_acceptance_rate": 24.796171570365118, "spec_decode_acceptance_length": 2.735732009925558, "spec_decode_num_drafts": 806, "spec_decode_draft_tokens": 5642, "spec_decode_accepted_tokens": 1399, "spec_decode_per_position_acceptance_rates": [0.6898263027295285, 0.3970223325062035, 0.2456575682382134, 0.15632754342431762, 0.1